  "reading": "GO on the engine. Joern builds a CPG for a pair tree in 5-30s, resolves the multi-hop flows the flat IR could not, and is deterministic: every verdict checked twice over one CPG agreed (deterministic_all=true). Entailment on the injection slice is 54% against the flat IR's 2.2% -- a 24x lift -- and 61.5% on the pairs where the differential question is well-posed. Every remaining gap is in OUR data model, not the engine, which is precisely the result that justifies adopting a CPG rather than building one.",
